    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe rule \"reject creating an owner when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners (409)\" is implemented as a new pipeline step on `POST /api/owners`, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `EnsureUniqueTelephone` / `EnsureUniqueHousehold` guard steps):\n\n1. **`EnsureCityCapacity`** (function) \u2014 reads the `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` request, counts existing owners whose city matches (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed), and throws `CityAtCapacityException` when the count is already \u2265 50.\n2. **`CityAtCapacityException`** (checked exception) \u2014 so it appears in the `throws` clause and routes through escalation.\n3. **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** + its escalation YAML \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with a `ProblemDetail`, same as the existing duplicate handlers.\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `ensureCityCapacity` in after `ensureUniqueHousehold` and before `build`, so the check runs before any persistence.\n\nThe pre-existing acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a fresh city to exactly 50, then expects the 51st to 409) now passes, and the full suite builds green.",
